# ============================================================================
# WARNING: do NOT have NODE_ENV or VITEST set in the shell(s) you use to run
# the e2e stack (`npm run seed`, `npm run start`, `npm run e2e`).
#
# src/server/lib/db.ts decides its database with:
#   useMemoryDb = process.env.NODE_ENV === 'test' || !!process.env.VITEST
# If EITHER is set, the server swaps to a brand-new in-memory PGlite and
# IGNORES DATABASE_URL below completely — it never touches the real e2e
# Postgres database at all, silently.
#
# `npm run seed` and `npm run start` are separate OS processes. If NODE_ENV or
# VITEST leaks into either one (parent shell, IDE task runner, a global env
# file some tool auto-loads, etc.), EACH process gets its OWN empty, throwaway
# PGlite: the seed script "succeeds" writing its admin user into a PGlite that
# vanishes when it exits, then the server boots against a second, different
# empty PGlite that never saw that seed. Net effect: no login exists, every
# Playwright spec fails at the sign-in step, and nothing in the failure output
# points back to this — it just looks like broken auth. Before running seed/
# start for e2e, confirm both are unset, e.g.:
#   node -e "console.log(process.env.NODE_ENV, process.env.VITEST)"
# should print: undefined undefined
# ============================================================================

# .env.e2e.example
#
# Documents every env var the Task-14 Playwright e2e stack reads. NOT auto-loaded by
# playwright.config.ts — this repo has no dotenv wiring anywhere (same as the root
# .env.example) — export these in your shell before `npm run e2e` only if you need to
# deviate from the defaults already baked into e2e/helpers/db.ts, e2e/reset-db.mjs, and
# playwright.config.ts's own webServer `env` blocks.

# Dedicated e2e Postgres. The database itself must already exist (e.g. `createdb
# mission_commander_e2e`) — e2e/reset-db.mjs only resets its schema (DROP/CREATE SCHEMA
# public), it does not create the database. MUST contain "e2e" in the name —
# reset-db.mjs refuses to run otherwise, since it drops a schema.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/mission_commander_e2e

# Port the API server (src/server/index.ts) listens on; also the health-check target
# for playwright.config.ts's API webServer entry. Hardcoded to 3002 there to match
# vite.config.ts's proxy default — change both together if you override this.
PORT=3002

# vite.config.ts's /api proxy target — must equal PORT above. Set on the Vite
# webServer entry, not the API entry.
API_PORT=3002

# better-auth's own baseURL (src/server/lib/auth.ts falls back to :3002 if unset).
BASE_URL=http://localhost:3002

# Extra origins better-auth's trustedOrigins() (src/server/lib/auth.ts) accepts,
# beyond its hardcoded :5173/:3002. playwright.config.ts sets this to the e2e Vite
# origin, :5274 — required so both bootstrapFirstAdmin's POST (e2e/helpers/auth.ts)
# and every real browser sign-in from the SPA pass better-auth's origin-check
# middleware instead of getting a 403 "Invalid origin".
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5274

# better-auth session/cookie signing secret. A throwaway value for the disposable e2e
# database only — never reuse this in a real environment.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=e2e-test-secret-not-for-production
